  "final_answer": "The 404 is fixed. The tests pass (exit code 0).\n\n**Cause:** `suggestions.ts` posted to `/api/recommend`, but the backend has no such route. The only recommendation endpoint is `POST /api/colleges/recommend`, defined in `python-backend/api/routes.py`.\n\nThere was a second bug behind the first. The backend's `RecommendRequest` requires a `student_profile` field, but the client sent a flat `{student_id, answers}` body. Fixing only the URL would have turned the 404 into a 422 error.\n\n**Fix:** I changed both fetch calls in `suggestions.ts`, in `generateSuggestedColleges` and `generateSuggestedCollegesFromAnswers`:\n- The URL is now `/api/colleges/recommend`.\n- The body is now `{ student_profile: { student_id, answers } }`. This is the same shape `collegeApi.ts` already sends.\n\nI didn't add a second `/api/recommend` route to the backend. The client was calling the wrong address, so I fixed the client.\n\n**Files changed:** only `client/src/services/college/suggestions.ts`.",
